 "audit": "Diagnosis labels are heterogeneous and overlapping (Rhabdomyosarcoma NOS vs Embryonal vs Alveolar; Glioma malignant vs Astrocytoma NOS vs Glioblastoma; Neoplasm malignant/uncertain; 81 missing and 25 Unknown diagnoses), so associations are split across labels and likely diluted or inflated by mix of subtypes. Extreme hypermutators (about 20 cases with >100 mutations, up to 15731, mostly Glioma malignant) were excluded since they create spurious gene hits; 124 cases have zero mutations, which may be sequencing/calling gaps. Recurrent identical variant C17orf80 p.S281R in 75 cases across diagnoses looks like an artifact or germline/batch contamination and was ignored. Several diagnoses have tiny n (<15), and exploratory ARID1B/ZMYM3/ASXL1/PIK3R1 hits are not clearly known and could be burden- or site-confounded (long genes, glioma and RMS have higher burden). Cohort is pooled from multiple sources with unknown batch/caller differences; no ancestry or treatment data.",
 "agent": "sonnet-neutral"
